  "final_message": "Wait for task `4db4c6a8-a0ee-40f2-9cc5-e3dd3b9fdc07/task-2` to complete.\nWaiting for task to complete.\nWaiting for the command to finish.\nWaiting for task to complete.\nWaiting for the task to finish.\nWaiting for task `task-45` to finish.\nWaiting for task `task-45` to finish.\nWaiting for task to complete.\nWaiting for command to finish.\nWaiting for task to finish.\nWaiting for git log to finish.\nWaiting for task.\nWaiting for task completion.\nWaiting for command to finish.\nWaiting for `npm test` to finish.\nWaiting for task to complete.\nWaiting for task notification.\nWaiting for npm test task to complete.\nWaiting for task-83 to complete.\nWaiting for task completion.\nWaiting for task 83 to complete.\nI have started `npm test` and am waiting for the test suite to finish running in the background.\nI cannot remove the `channel` field from the [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) event or the order model due to architecture rule **ARCH-4** defined in [GEMINI.md](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/GEMINI.md#L27):\n\n> **ARCH-4**: `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\n### Key Reasons:\n1. **External Contract Breakage**: Even though no internal components within `orders-service` read `channel`, [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) is an external contract consumed by external downstream services (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`). Removing the field would break deployed consumers.\n2. **Deprecation Policy**: Under ARCH-4, schema changes must be additive. Any removal or rename of event fields must first go through a formal deprecation lifecycle across the consuming services before the field can be removed.\n3. **Model Dependency**: The [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) domain model supplies the `channel` property when publishing the event in [`orderPlaced()`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59). Removing it from the domain model would prevent populating the event.\n",
